# Update Release Notes Workflow

## Purpose
This workflow automates the creation and update of release notes in RELEASES.md based on git commits since the last release date. When a new release section is written, the version date in the filter bar is updated to match.

## How to Use
Run the command: `update-release-notes` or ask Cursor to "update release notes"

## Workflow Steps

1. **Read RELEASES.md** to find the date of the most recent release (look for the latest "## Release YYYY-MM-DD" heading)

2. **Get git commits** since that date:
   ```bash
   git log --since="<last-release-date>" --pretty=format:"%h|%s|%an" --date=short --no-merges
   ```

3. **Analyze commits** and categorize them into:
   - **Nieuwe features** (🪄): New functionality, new pages, new components
   - **Verbeteringen** (✨): UI/UX improvements, performance improvements
   - **Bug fixes** (🐛): Bug fixes and error corrections
   - **Technische wijzigingen** (🧹): Refactoring, code cleanup, technical improvements
   - **Diverse**: Other changes

4. **Group by feature area** when applicable:
   - Prestaties aanbieders
   - Gebruikersinterface
   - Kaart
   - Aanbod
   - Zones/Beleidszones
   - Servicegebieden
   - Export
   - etc.

5. **Write release notes in Dutch** following the format:
   ```markdown
   ## Release YYYY-MM-DD
   
   **Feature Area** (if applicable)
   
   - 🪄 Description of new feature in Dutch
   - ✨ Description of improvement in Dutch
   - 🐛 Description of bug fix in Dutch
   - 🧹 Description of technical change in Dutch
   ```

6. **Insert the new release section** at the top of RELEASES.md, right after the "# Dashboard Deelmobiliteit app Releases" heading

7. **If a new release section was created**, update the version date in the filter bar to the same `YYYY-MM-DD` date. In `src/components/Filterbar/Filterbar.tsx`, replace only the date text inside the version link (the `<a>` that points to `RELEASES.md`). Keep the surrounding markup unchanged. Example:

   ```tsx
   Versie{' '}
   <a
     href="https://github.com/Stichting-CROW/dashboarddeelmobiliteit-app/blob/main/RELEASES.md#dashboard-deelmobiliteit-app-releases"
     target="_blank"
     rel="external noreferrer"
     className="underline"
   >
     YYYY-MM-DD
   </a>
   ```

   Do this only when new release notes were actually written. If there are no new commits to document, leave both files unchanged.

8. **Use appropriate emojis**:
   - 🪄 for new features
   - ✨ for improvements
   - 🐛 for bug fixes
   - 🧹 for technical/refactoring changes

## Rules

- All release notes must be in **Dutch**
- Use clear, user-friendly language (not too technical)
- Group related changes together
- Use the current date as the release date (format: YYYY-MM-DD)
- The filter bar version date in `src/components/Filterbar/Filterbar.tsx` must match that release date
- Include context about what changed and why it matters to users
- For technical changes, explain the user-facing impact if any
- Keep descriptions concise but informative

## Example Output Format

```markdown
## Release 2026-01-29

**Prestaties aanbieders**

- 🪄 Nieuwe pagina 'Prestaties aanbieders' voor het monitoren van prestaties van aanbieders
- 🪄 Nieuwe detailpagina met grafieken voor gedetailleerde analyse

**Gebruikersinterface**

- 🪄 Tooltips zijn nu klikbaar: klik op het tooltip-icoon om de tooltip te openen
- ✨ Elke pagina heeft nu een specifieke paginatitel in de browser

**Kaart**

- 🐛 Opgelost: Browser console errors in MapComponent zijn verholpen
```

## Commit Message Patterns to Recognize

- `feat(...)`: New feature → 🪄
- `fix(...)`: Bug fix → 🐛
- `refactor(...)`: Refactoring → 🧹
- `style(...)`: Styling changes → ✨
- `chore(...)`: Maintenance → 🧹
- `perf(...)`: Performance → ✨
- `docs(...)`: Documentation → ✨

## Notes

- Skip merge commits (they're usually just "Merge pull request #X")
- Combine related commits into single bullet points when appropriate
- Focus on user-facing changes, but include important technical improvements
- If a commit message is unclear, look at the actual code changes to understand what was done
- When new release notes are written, always update the filter bar version date in the same change
